Rocket in Cloud's one change to JSRM v3.3 (github.com/jbgust/jsrm, GPL-3.0), 24 November 2026.
Applied by scripts/build-web-jars.sh before JSRM is built; jsrm-web.jar carries this file in META-INF.

Why: for a shaped grain (C-slot, finocyl, moon burner, star), JSRM redraws the grain's burned-back
cross-section with java.awt.geom at every calculation line. A simulation first asks for every
cross-section area (for the grain volume) and later for every burning area, so each cross-section
was drawn three times: once for its area, then again with the one 0.001 mm further on for the
burning area. Now the burning area is worked out the first time, measuring the same cross-section
on the way, and both numbers are kept: two drawings per line instead of three.

Results: none change. Every number JSRM gives, for the eight test motors of
web/test/fixtures/jsrm-native.json (every grain shape and propellant), simulations and Kn-table
areas alike, is byte-for-byte the same as unpatched JSRM's (in Java 17). In the browser (CheerpJ, Chrome, median of three): star 17.5 s -> 13.1 s,
finocyl 11.2 s -> 9.3 s, C-slot and moon burner 2.6 s -> 2.4 s.

